{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Sweep continuation — 2026-09-20T11:40Z\n\n### Tickets closed (4, all with signed completion attestations)\n\n| Ticket | Alias | Merged SHA |\n|---|---|---|\n| `bc25-1351-dd0e-4909` | thorough-hexed-ferret | `cc4a23a2405b752a0d9587720f9295ec72871372` |\n| `c6fb-49cf-61e3-4b29` | selective-dermic-coelacanth | `3fac858d3c4edffbbc15d6eccfb7ad1b085cbe7b` |\n| `859c-760d-04dd-44a6` | trifling-countable-armadillo | `feca8a211eea97ad21859a1494bb57dab1e15988` |\n| `974f-a1c8-da40-43a0` | picky-carefree-dragonfly | `e84e4c5e9439bcfd27875d152de36eb40eb4f46b` |\n\nEvery Gerrit change landed this session is now merged AND its ticket closed. 0 open Gerrit\nchanges.\n\n### Live production verification of landed fixes\n\n- **bc25** — `Verify Authorship Identity` run `35505599913` on the merged SHA: `success`,\n  with the log reporting `SIZE_PACK_KIB: 23460` against the restored `102400` budget. The\n  workflow's `branches-ignore` list contains `main`, so a merge can never trigger it; it\n  must be dispatched manually.\n- **974f** — `Mirror Guard` run `35507233659` on the merged SHA: `success`. The 4 preceding\n  runs also succeeded.\n- **859c** — `Terraform Drift` dispatched as run `35507409132` on the merged tip. The\n  **failure mode changed**, which is the proof: pre-fix run `35494675507` died with 4 x\n  `Error: No value for required variable` (the plan never ran); post-fix the plan runs to\n  completion and reports `Plan: 1 to add, 4 to change, 0 to destroy`. The residual red is\n  genuine unapplied drift, tracked by `3d85-eaad-b5e0-4f84`, which needs a human decision\n  because it would delete the `AllowCostAlerts` SNS statement.\n\n### Process correction: I cancelled a healthy CI run\n\nRun `35502010162`'s Jira DC harness job was `in_progress` at 6,748s while its 9 sibling\njobs had finished in ~2 minutes. I judged it hung and cancelled it to release its logs.\n\n**It was not hung.** The last green run of that job took **6252.74s** for the same step\n(`74 passed, 1 skipped, 1 xfailed ... in 6252.74s (1:44:12)`). The cancelled run was at\n**1.08x** that.\n\nTwo contributing defects, both now tracked as `2277-7043-1f63-4f5c`\n(`juiced-useful-shrike`):\n\n1. The step's calibration comment claims `2384-2635s over 63 tests`. Measured: `6252.74s`\n   over `76` tests. Stale by ~2.4x, so a normal run reads as 2.6x over budget.\n2. The step emits **no output whatsoever** until it exits — the green run's entire step log\n   carries exactly `1` distinct timestamp. There is no progress signal available to\n   contradict the stale comment.\n\nRoot cause of (2), established by single-variable experiment rather than inference:\n`PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1` changes nothing (**refuted**), while `-v` instead of `-q` streams one\nline per test at the true cadence (**confirmed**). Under `-q` pytest writes newline-less\nprogress dots, and GitHub Actions' line-oriented reader has no complete line to stamp until\nthe process exits.\n\nCost of the error: ~1h52m of live-Jira execution destroyed, and `6d98-28f4-946a-4016`'s AC3\nevidence lost. Remediated by re-dispatching `external-integration.yml` against current\n`main` as run `35508005436`.\n\n### GitHub Actions state\n\n- `Mirror Guard` — green.\n- `Verify Authorship Identity` — green (dispatched).\n- `Terraform Drift` — red, and correctly so: real drift, owned by `3d85`, human decision.\n- `Live External Integration` — re-running as `35508005436`; the DC harness lane needs\n  ~1h45m-2h10m.\n- Logs for the 2026-09-14 DC harness failure (job `103878992643`) are no longer\n  retrievable (`BlobNotFound`), so that failure cannot be retro-diagnosed.\n\n### Open\n\n- `6d98-28f4-946a-4016` — `in_progress`, blocked on run `35508005436` concluding.\n- `2277-7043-1f63-4f5c` — new P2, plan review running.\n- `3d85-eaad-b5e0-4f84` — needs a human decision on applying the Terraform plan.\n- 13 user-deferred bugs, unchanged."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789904461284659065,"uuid":"1b22a15c-ad50-470e-b9a6-43692878bba4"}